#: ../../source/docs/skyviper.rst:211
#: 416533d65a1e4c35b963f3ce3e234ab6
msgid "Mode1/Mode2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/skyviper.rst:213
#: 481f67f04dc34bd2bbdb1cb2fb352806
msgid "The default TX stick mapping is mode2. To change to mode1, go to the Flight Parameters page in the web interface (``http://192.168.99.1/parameters.html``) and choose the Radio category. Change ``BRD_RADIO_STKMD`` to your preferred RC mode. Modes 1, 2, 3 and 4 are supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/skyviper.rst:216
#: 4bf4a6fe9389439cbc35ed220bf4500e
msgid "Disabling RX Telemetry"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/skyviper.rst:218
#: 04864b5667ea4e9aa0389ed3d5923d20
msgid "You can temporarily disable telemetry from the drone by setting the ``BRD_RADIO_TELEM`` parameters to zero. See the parameters page at http://192.168.99.1/parameters.html"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/skyviper.rst:220
#: 0c6cb93b3a804cd19202e530c255bbd3
msgid "When telemetry is disabled the TX will beep constantly as it tries to find the drone, and won’t update the buzzer or LEDs for fight mode changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/skyviper.rst:224
#: 16a6cf37e83d4372a7f98c708787b155
msgid "Factory Test Mode for TX/RX"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/skyviper.rst:226
#: 950c268b2dda4956afd030f6b93b32a9
msgid "To facilitate rapid testing of transmitters in the factory there is a special factory test mode. This mode avoids the need to bind each transmitter, and gives fast startup on fixed channels. Factory test mode can be setup for up to 8 test stations in the factory. Each test station should have its own test copter. To setup a copter for factory test mode you need to set a receiving copter as the test copter for a particular test station. You do this by setting the ``BRD_RADIO_TESTCH`` parameter in the Radio parameters on ``http://192.168.99.1/parameters.html`` to a factory testing station number. This can be:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/skyviper.rst:243
#: fbd954f4c4a04fb38975732aaf6ab869
msgid "You must reboot after setting this parameter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/skyviper.rst:245
#: 378cb042bfcd4acd9c1ec98bdb793fb3
msgid "To test a transmitter you need to boot it into test mode for the right test station. To do this you need to power on the transmitter with the left shoulder button pressed, and with the left stick in one of 4 possible positions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/skyviper.rst:258
#: 0e604011b0a5429b9bac7ab1357b80d3
msgid "When you startup in factory test mode the transmitter will play a different buzzer tune, and will bind immediately with the receiver. You can then do rapid testing on the Transmitter tab of the status page on the web interface at ``http://192.168.99.1/status.html``. Each test station uses a different set of channels, so are unlikely to interfere with each other."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/skyviper.rst:264
#: b67ea5246fb64a8bb663a095d7b50aac
msgid "Log Files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/skyviper.rst:266
#: 6c19ed21ff1843f1aa74d488b3d444cf
msgid "DataFlash logs are stored on the microSD card of the Sonix in the DATAFLASH directory. You can access them via the filesystem interface of the web interface. In order to enable logging while Disarmed, go to the web interface Flight Parameters page, select Logging, in the drop-down, and set LOG_DISARMED to 1:ENABLED."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/skyviper.rst:268
#: 04f7f4f6684943149b2cd3dc3eb2b1df
msgid "Logs are binary files and can be viewed in several log viewers, including MissionPlanner."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/skyviper.rst:271
#: 80411426c4414c8c8051650ee97098d6
msgid "Factory Reset"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/skyviper.rst:273
#: e27e1a0d765e4cf5bc698f9931e7d3b9
msgid "If all else fails put a file called ``FACRESET.TXT`` in the root of the microSD. It should do a factory reset on next boot."
